# TODOS File Conventions

<rule>
actions:
  - type: information
    message: |
      ## Todos File Structure
      
      When creating or updating a todos file, follow this structure:
      
      ```markdown
      # {TICKET_ID}: {TICKET_TITLE}
      
      ## Figma Designs
      
      When the ticket includes Figma links (REQUIRED steps):
      - [ ] Review Figma designs using `mcp_figma_getDesign` tool
      - [ ] Download ALL key assets using `mcp_figma_downloadImages` tool
      - [ ] **REQUIRED**: Store all design assets in `api-plans/assets/{TICKET_ID}/` directory
      - [ ] Reference specific node IDs and states in implementation tasks
      - [ ] Ensure implementation exactly matches Figma specifications
      
      ## Commit 1: {DESCRIPTIVE TITLE}
      
      - [ ] Task 1 description
      - [ ] Task 2 description
        ```typescript
        // Example code if needed
        ```
      - [ ] Task 3 description
      - [ ] Update tests in `tests/path/to/relevant_file.test.ts`:
        - Follow `zc-testing-conventions.mdc` rule
        - Ensure test coverage for changes
      
      ## Commit 2: {DESCRIPTIVE TITLE}
      
      - [ ] Task 1 description
      - [ ] Task 2 description
      - [ ] Task 3 description
      - [ ] Update tests in `tests/path/to/relevant_file.test.ts`
      ```
      
      ## Definition of Done for Tasks
      
      A task is considered complete ONLY when:
      
      1. The source code changes have been implemented correctly
      2. The corresponding test files have been updated:
         - For source file at `src/path/to/file.ts`, test file at `tests/path/to/file.test.ts` must be updated
         - Tests must follow the `zc-testing-conventions.mdc` rule
         - New functionality must be covered by tests
      3. All test execution requirements are met:
         - All tests related to the current task have been executed
         - All tests pass successfully
         - Test results have been documented in the completion checklist
      4. All code quality requirements are met:
         - Linting checks have been run on all modified code
         - All linting errors or warnings have been resolved
         - Linting status has been documented in the completion checklist
      5. The task is marked as complete in the todos file with the checkbox checked `[x]`
      6. Test updates are documented in the todos file
      7. User feedback has been received and incorporated:
         - Always wait for explicit user feedback before considering a task done
         - Treat user feedback as a code review that may require additional changes
         - Do not move to the next task until current changes are approved
      
      ## Task Completion Checklist
      
      Before marking any task as complete, document the following:
      
      ```
      ## Task Completion Checklist
      
      - [x] Implementation meets all functional requirements
      - [x] Tests run: [command used]
        - Result: All tests passing (X passed, 0 failed)
      - [x] Linting checks: [command used]
        - Result: No linting errors/warnings
      - [x] Documentation updated (if applicable)
      ```
      
      ## Creating Task Items
      
      When creating task items:
      
      1. Break down implementation into small, focused tasks
      2. Include explicit test update tasks for each file modified
      3. Include code snippets where helpful
      4. Define clear boundaries between tasks
      5. Always include test updates as part of the task's Definition of Done

examples:

- input: |
  Create a todos file for ticket ID-12345
  output: |
  # ID-12345: Feature Title
  
  ## Figma Designs
  - [ ] Review Figma designs at https://www.figma.com/file/example/design using `mcp_figma_getDesign`
  - [ ] Download ALL UI components using `mcp_figma_downloadImages` tool
  - [ ] **REQUIRED**: Store all design assets in `api-plans/assets/ID-12345/` directory
  - [ ] Reference specific node IDs in implementation tasks
  - [ ] Ensure implementation exactly matches Figma specifications
  
  ## Commit 1: Update user authentication
  - [ ] Add new authentication provider to AuthService
  - [ ] Update UserService to use new provider
  - [ ] Update tests in tests/services/user.service.test.ts:
    - Follow `zc-testing-conventions.mdc` rule
    - Add test cases for new auth flow
  ## Commit 2: Add UI components
  - [ ] Create new login form component
  - [ ] Add routing for authentication pages
  - [ ] Update tests in tests/components/login-form.test.ts
  - [ ] Update tests in tests/components/login-form.test.ts